<p>The fetch failed, but the feed carried the whole piece, so the archive keeps
that instead of keeping nothing at all. A feed body is a worse source than the
page — it usually lacks images and the canonical structure — but it is very much
better than an empty row where an article should be.</p>
<p>This rung exists because the alternative is losing the article entirely when
a site goes down between publication and the next poll, which is exactly when
archiving matters most and exactly when fetching is least likely to work.</p>
